{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2252","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2252","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2252\",\"parent_revision\":\"cc5d41211678119b62041ff0720cea32c8d983c0\",\"root_revision\":\"2f271e61f27ab10cc692d6b351e031ab8714d9cffe0d5aabbef7c4fbc3b29275\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims verified against primary sources. Training data recall excluded as evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 1**: `code-reviewer.md` Step 2 (lines 52\u201358) uses Glob/Grep only with no git fallback, returns BLOCKED when no files can be identified.\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Step 2 returns STATUS: BLOCKED when no files can be identified from task body\\nevidence: Read tool \u2014 plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md lines 51\u201359:\\n  \\\"Use Glob and Grep to identify the files changed or added by this task.\\n   If no files can be identified, return STATUS: BLOCKED with a request for explicit file paths.\\\"\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md lines 51\u201359 (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 2**: brooks-lint `common.md` lines 81\u201394 demonstrates the fallback chain: `git diff --cached` \u2192 `git diff` \u2192 `git diff main...HEAD` \u2192 ask user.\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Research file documents PR Review mode auto-scope detection as: cached \u2192 working \u2192 main...HEAD \u2192 ask\\nevidence: Read tool \u2014 research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md lines 254\u2013265:\\n  \\\"PR Review: git diff --cached \u2192 git diff \u2192 git diff main...HEAD \u2192 ask user.\\n   Reports always state detected scope explicitly.\\\"\\nsource: research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md lines 254\u2013265 (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 3**: CLAUDE.md principle states agents must NOT have file paths pre-discovered on their behalf.\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: CLAUDE.md instructs \\\"Do NOT discover file paths on behalf of agents\\\"\\nevidence: CLAUDE.md system content (loaded at session start):\\n  \\\"Do NOT discover file paths on behalf of agents \u2014 the agent has full tool access\\n   and an empty context window; it finds what it needs itself.\\\"\\nsource: .claude/CLAUDE.md (loaded 2026-05-29)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 4**: Output Format STATUS block does not contain a `Scope:` field.\\n\\n```\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Output Format STATUS block (lines 241\u2013256) has no Scope: field\\nevidence: Read tool \u2014 plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md lines 239\u2013257:\\n  STATUS block contains: SUMMARY, ARTIFACTS, RISKS, NOTES \u2014 no Scope: field present\\nsource: plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md lines 239\u2013257 (accessed 2026-05-29)\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Claim 5**: `git diff origin/main...HEAD` should fall back to `git diff HEAD~1...HEAD` when `origin/main` is not reachable (AC #8).\\n\\n```\\nverdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\nclaim: AC #8 specifies origin/main fallback to HEAD~1...HEAD\\nevidence: No existing precedent found in codebase for this specific fallback pattern.\\n  Standard git behavior: git diff origin/main...HEAD fails with \\\"unknown revision\\\" when\\n  origin/main is absent. HEAD~1...HEAD is a valid safe substitute.\\nsource: AC #8 of backlog item #2252 \u2014 design decision, not verifiable from existing code\\nnote: INCONCLUSIVE \u2192 DERIVABLE. Fallback is reasonable standard practice but requires\\n  the implementer to decide on the exact error-detection mechanism.\\n```\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: code-review: Auto-scope detection from git state when delegation prompt omits file list\\nDate: 2026-05-29\\nGoal: Add four-step git fallback chain to code-reviewer.md Step 2 so agent self-detects scope when delegation prompt omits file list\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent \u2014 Step 2 returns BLOCKED instead of querying git state; fallback chain specified | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read code-reviewer.md lines 51\u201359 confirmed current behavior\\n2. Scope boundaries \u2014 exactly one file: code-reviewer.md Step 2 and Output Format section | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Impact Radius analysis confirms single-file, two-section change\\n3. External interfaces \u2014 git diff --cached, git diff, git diff origin/main...HEAD | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: brooks-lint.md lines 254\u2013265 (Read, 2026-05-29)\\n4. Constraints \u2014 explicit-file-list path unchanged; CLAUDE.md agent self-discovery principle | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: CLAUDE.md session content verified\\n5. Existing system context \u2014 code-reviewer.md Step 2 lines 51\u201359 | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tool verbatim output lines 51\u201359\\n6. Verification expectations \u2014 Step 2 four-step chain; STATUS Scope: line | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Output Format confirmed lines 183\u2013256; no Scope: field present \u2014 gap confirmed\\n7. AC #8 fallback design \u2014 origin/main fallback to HEAD~1...HEAD | Snapshot: not present \u2192 Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: Fact-Check claim 5 INCONCLUSIVE \u2014 standard git practice; implementer decides exact error-detection mechanism\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- Condition 7 (AC #8 fallback): (new) DERIVABLE \u2014 discovered by fact-checker; not a blocker for planning\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 6\\nDERIVABLE count: 1\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **code-review: auto-scope detection from git state when delegation prompt omits file list** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md \u2014 pattern: auto-scope detection (cached \u2192 diff \u2192 main...HEAD \u2192 ask)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-17)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n7/10 \u2014 Removes a class of false BLOCKED states that forces orchestrators to pre-discover files before every dispatch. Directly contradicts CLAUDE.md principle. P1 is correct: affects every orchestrator using `@dh:code-reviewer` on branch-implied scope.\\n\\n**Effort**: Small \u2014 single file edit to `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md`. Step 2 text replaced with fallback chain (~10 lines). Output Format section gains one `Scope:` field definition. No Python, no MCP, no schema changes.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- **Blocks**: Every orchestrator that dispatches `@dh:code-reviewer` on a task that does not enumerate files in the body \u2014 the common case when branch implies scope\\n- **Bottleneck**: Forces orchestrators to run file-discovery steps before dispatch, duplicating work the agent could perform itself\\n- **Friction**: Produces confusing BLOCKED states for what should be routine reviews\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Orchestrators can dispatch `@dh:code-reviewer` without pre-discovering file paths \u2014 agent self-scopes from git state\\n- Removes a class of false BLOCKED states that currently require orchestrator intervention\\n- Adds explicit `Scope:` traceability to every review STATUS output, making scope visible and auditable\\n- Aligns code-reviewer scope detection with the established brooks-lint pattern\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen a delegation prompt does not list explicit files, `code-reviewer.md` Step 2 attempts each git fallback in sequence and proceeds with the first non-empty result. The Scope level used (explicit, staged, working, branch) is recorded in the STATUS output block. If all four levels yield no files, the agent returns STATUS: BLOCKED. The orchestrator is never required to pre-discover files on behalf of the agent.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nStep 2 of `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` contains a four-step fallback chain:\\n\\n1. Files explicit in delegation prompt \u2014 use those\\n2. `git diff --cached` \u2014 if non-empty, use those files\\n3. `git diff` \u2014 if non-empty, use those files\\n4. `git diff origin/main...HEAD` \u2014 if non-empty, use those files\\n5. None found \u2014 STATUS: BLOCKED requesting explicit file paths\\n\\nThe Output Format section includes a `Scope:` field in the STATUS block indicating which fallback level was used (`explicit | staged | working | branch | blocked`).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 2 contains the four-step fallback chain (explicit \u2192 staged \u2192 working \u2192 branch \u2192 BLOCKED)\\n2. The Output Format STATUS block includes a `Scope:` line with values `explicit | staged | working | branch | blocked`\\n3. When a delegation prompt includes explicit file paths, the agent uses those and records `Scope: explicit` \u2014 existing behavior unchanged\\n4. When a delegation prompt omits file paths and `git diff --cached` is non-empty, agent records `Scope: staged`\\n5. When `git diff --cached` is empty and `git diff` is non-empty, agent records `Scope: working`\\n6. When both `git diff --cached` and `git diff` are empty and `git diff origin/main...HEAD` is non-empty, agent records `Scope: branch`\\n7. When all three git commands return empty output, agent returns STATUS: BLOCKED\\n8. `git diff origin/main...HEAD` falls back to `git diff HEAD~1...HEAD` when `origin/main` is not reachable\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work (reference pattern) | `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` lines 254\u2013265 \u2014 auto-scope detection fallback chain (VERIFIED 2026-05-29) |\\n| File to modify | `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 2 (lines 51\u201359) and Output Format Status block (lines 239\u2013257) |\\n| Principle violated (current) | `.claude/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 \\\"Do NOT discover file paths on behalf of agents\\\" (VERIFIED 2026-05-29) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 self-contained change to one agent file\\n- Blocks: None identified. Items that dispatch `@dh:code-reviewer` benefit immediately once this change ships\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 single file edit to `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md`. Step 2 text (lines 51\u201359) replaced with four-step fallback chain (~15 lines). Output Format Status block (lines 239\u2013257) gains one `Scope:` field. No Python, no MCP, no schema changes. Estimated: 30 minutes.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 the agent file is the primary change target (Step 2 text + Output Format Status block)\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\nNone. All required inputs available. Single-file change with no dependencies.\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:d0a31a250c224a01b2a167ad6d4de7e5 -->\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\nNone identified. The STATUS response gains an additive `Scope:` field \u2014 backward-compatible with all existing orchestrator callers.\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` \u2014 dispatches `@dh:code-reviewer` at Step 2 (line 62) via `task_file_path` + `item_id`; does not pre-discover files \u2014 benefits from this fix without requiring changes\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` \u2014 references `@dh:code-reviewer` dispatch; no file pre-discovery in dispatch path; no change needed\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md::Step 2` \u2014 currently uses Glob/Grep only, returns BLOCKED when no files identified; change: replace with four-step git fallback chain (explicit \u2192 staged \u2192 working \u2192 branch \u2192 BLOCKED)\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified. No schema changes, no MCP changes, no CI workflow changes.\\n\\n### Current State\\n\\nStep 2 (\\\"Identify Files Under Review\\\") of `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` (lines 52\u201358) instructs the agent to use `Glob` and `Grep` to find files mentioned in the task body or acceptance criteria. The final instruction is: \\\"If no files can be identified, return STATUS: BLOCKED with a request for explicit file paths.\\\"\\n\\nThere is no git fallback path. When a delegation prompt omits an explicit file list \u2014 the common case when a branch's changed files are implied by `git diff` \u2014 the agent returns BLOCKED immediately, forcing the orchestrator to pre-discover files before dispatch. This contradicts CLAUDE.md: \\\"Do NOT discover file paths on behalf of agents \u2014 the agent has full tool access and an empty context window; it finds what it needs itself.\\\"\\n\\nThe reference pattern exists at `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` lines 254\u2013265 (sourced from brooks-lint `common.md` lines 81\u201394): PR Review mode runs `git diff --cached` \u2192 `git diff` \u2192 `git diff main...HEAD` \u2192 ask user. Reports always state detected scope explicitly.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: DIVERGENT\\n\\n**Design intent**: CLAUDE.md establishes that agents are self-sufficient \u2014 they have full tool access and an empty context window, and should find what they need themselves. Orchestrators are explicitly prohibited from pre-discovering file paths on behalf of agents.\\n\\n**Current implementation**: `code-reviewer.md` Step 2 does not self-discover scope from git state. When the delegation prompt omits an explicit file list, the agent immediately returns STATUS: BLOCKED \u2014 it never attempts to use `Bash(git diff --cached)` or similar git commands to detect its own scope. This contradicts the agent self-discovery principle.\\n\\n**Divergence detail**:\\n| Dimension | Design Intent | Current State |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Agent self-discovery | Agent finds what it needs without orchestrator pre-discovery | Requires orchestrator to pre-discover files before dispatch |\\n| Fallback behavior | Self-rescue via available tools before blocking | Immediate BLOCKED \u2014 no fallback attempted |\\n| Scope traceability | Scope source should be visible in output | No `Scope:` field in STATUS output |\\n\\n**Reference**: brooks-lint `common.md` lines 81\u201394 demonstrates correct alignment \u2014 PR Review mode auto-detects scope through the same git fallback chain being proposed here.\\n\\n**Resolution**: This item's proposed change (four-step fallback chain + `Scope:` STATUS field) restores alignment with CLAUDE.md's agent self-discovery principle. After implementation: ALIGNED.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md::Output Format::Status Output` (lines 241\u2013256) \u2014 STATUS block template lacks `Scope:` field; gains `Scope: explicit|staged|working|branch|blocked` line\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [x] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [x] Every code consumer migrated to new interface (additive \u2014 no migration needed)\\n- [x] Every stale document updated (Output Format section gains Scope: field)\\n- [x] Every agent instruction updated (same file \u2014 code-reviewer.md)\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (not applicable \u2014 BLOCKED path retained as final fallback)\\n- [x] CI/config files updated and validated (no CI/config changes required)\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n**SDLC layer blast radius:**\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The system permits a false BLOCKED state when the code-reviewer agent cannot identify files from the task body. A git-state detection fallback chain (a guardrail) would prevent this outcome \u2014 the agent has full tool access but was never instructed to use it. No typo/surface fix. Same problem class has not appeared previously in this agent. The failure is traceable (missing instructions) but the root cause is a gate that was never built rather than a defect in an existing gate.\\n**Analysis Method**: none (missing-guardrail classification requires no additional RCA method)\\n**Scenario Target**: Delegation prompt with no explicit file list + branch with staged/unstaged changes \u2192 BLOCKED state \u2192 fix: agent self-detects scope from git state, returns `Scope: staged` or `Scope: working` or `Scope: branch`\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-FOR-PLANNING**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item description \u2014 Step 2 returns BLOCKED instead of querying git state; fallback chain specified |\\n| Scope boundaries | AVAILABLE | Exactly one file: `plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md`, Step 2 and Output Format section only |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | `git diff --cached`, `git diff`, `git diff origin/main...HEAD` \u2014 standard git commands |\\n| Constraints | AVAILABLE | Explicit-file-list path must remain unchanged; CLAUDE.md agent self-discovery principle must be respected |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | code-reviewer.md Step 2 (lines 52\u201358) confirmed via Read: uses Glob/Grep only, no git fallback, returns BLOCKED when no files identified |\\n| Verification expectations | AVAILABLE | Step 2 contains four-step chain; STATUS output includes `Scope:` line; agent run succeeds on empty task + non-empty `git diff --cached` |\\n\\nNo MISSING conditions. No blockers. Proceed to planning.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n**Feature item** \u2014 not a defect. Reproducibility is N/A for functional completeness verification.\\n\\nHowever, the absence can be observed:\\n\\n1. Dispatch `@dh:code-reviewer` on any SAM task whose task body does not enumerate explicit file paths and whose branch has changed files (non-empty `git diff`).\\n2. The agent returns `STATUS: BLOCKED` with \\\"request for explicit file paths\\\" rather than self-detecting scope.\\n3. Expected after fix: agent returns `STATUS: DONE` with `Scope: staged` or `Scope: working` or `Scope: branch` in the STATUS block.\\n\\nObservable signal: the `Scope:` field presence and value in the STATUS output block.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Role | Connection | Change needed |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 2 | Producer \u2014 identifies files under review | Direct implementation | Yes \u2014 add git fallback chain |\\n| `agents/code-reviewer.md` Output Format | Producer \u2014 STATUS block format | Additive field | Yes \u2014 add `Scope:` field |\\n| `skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | Consumer \u2014 dispatches code-reviewer | Dispatch orchestration | No \u2014 benefits automatically |\\n| `skills/forensic-review/SKILL.md` | Consumer \u2014 references code-reviewer | Reference | No \u2014 no file pre-discovery |\\n| `research/coding-agents/brooks-lint.md` | Prior work \u2014 reference pattern | Source of fallback chain design | No \u2014 reference only |\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nStep 2 of `agents/code-reviewer.md` updates to a fallback chain modeled on common.md lines 81\u201394:\\n\\n```text\\n1. Files explicit in delegation prompt? \u2192 use those\\n2. Else: git diff --cached \u2192 if non-empty, use those files\\n3. Else: git diff \u2192 if non-empty, use those files\\n4. Else: git diff origin/main...HEAD \u2192 if non-empty, use those files\\n5. Else: STATUS: BLOCKED with request for explicit file paths\\n```\\n\\nThe agent's STATUS output includes a \\\"Scope\\\" line stating which fallback level was used (`Scope: explicit | staged | working | branch | blocked`) so the orchestrator can verify the scope was correct.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 2 contains the four-step fallback chain by name. Output Format includes a \\\"Scope\\\" line in the STATUS block. Running the agent on a task with no file list and a non-empty `git diff --cached` produces a successful review citing the staged files in the artifact and a `Scope: staged` STATUS line.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/agents/code-reviewer.md` Step 2 (\\\"Identify Files Under Review\\\") instructs the agent: \\\"Use `Glob` and `Grep` to identify the files changed or added by this task. Patterns to search: source files mentioned in the task body or acceptance criteria, test files corresponding to changed source, configuration or schema files touched by the task. If no files can be identified, return STATUS: BLOCKED with a request for explicit file paths.\\\"\\n\\nThere is no fallback chain that consults git state. If the task body does not list files explicitly, the agent returns BLOCKED rather than examining `git diff --cached`, `git diff`, or `git diff origin/main...HEAD`. This forces every dispatch to pre-discover files \u2014 duplicating work and creating an explicit failure mode for tasks where the files-changed list is implied by the branch.\\n\\nThis conflicts with the CLAUDE.md guidance: \\\"Do NOT discover file paths on behalf of agents \u2014 the agent has full tool access and an empty context window; it finds what it needs itself.\\\"\\n\\nbrooks-lint's auto-scope detection (common.md lines 81\u201394) demonstrates the correct fallback chain: cached diff \u2192 working diff \u2192 branch diff \u2192 ask user. Reports always state detected scope explicitly.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c5ee16ef1b34fd383368e7e3db752e9ac71c19ac19d2c64ce9ca01da712fa118\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg21aA\"}"}